                                        "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                        "entry_id": "220154ff-7994-3422-9250-ce8aa081a3c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inclined to telling (by explicitly stating facts), instead of showing (by conveying an impression so that events are described in the narrative)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f86273a5-ee81-4e55-bc07-1bf86b28c094",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "I think my problem with it is that it's\na) a little \"telly\" not \"showy\" in comparison to the rest […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "360a36f4-8712-4413-94d9-9ad7a44fc836",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "There's a way to make this more showy and less telly. It's like you're in a hurry to get on with the rest of the story."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a6f7a52-c7e0-403a-83fe-6e54296921bd",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "story is too, too telly; need at least 3 showy scenes to improve showing:telling ratio"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87269a98-03f3-4fe5-b047-0c4fa040e70f",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "Six of Crows is very telly and little showy. You are constantly getting info dumps and mini-flashbacks to the characters past."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52f578b8-32f1-46ae-aa91-06689e673602",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "The only other objection I have—and again, it’s minor—is that the very last chapter feels very “telly” and rushed. I get why, but a smoother exit would have really made an otherwise wonderful book almost perfect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "462c0366-b570-43ee-b63b-7aad1450be5a",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "Lee’s style of narration reads like an old-style fairy tale to an extent—it’s very telly, if that makes any sense. We get descriptions of character actions and we’re told about character motives as filtered through the third-person narrator, but we don’t actually get to read these characters’ thoughts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "500da68a-4a58-4f60-a8e9-da382ef3c4d6",
                                                "sense_id": "0aea72c7-882f-330c-b5b5-191ce6530226",
                                                "text": "The ending felt rushed to me, and I wish it would have been more showy and less telly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
